{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"61baf8e7b102a6b3","name":"card_unit_panzer_iii_j_late","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BloodIron/units/card_unit_panzer_iii_j_late","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PANZER III-J LATE","text":"Becomes Veteran when the enemy HQ has taken 4 or more damage.","flavorText":"The Panzer III Ausf. J was the most common variant of the Panzer III, a German medium tank widely used in WWII. Initially designed as an anti-tank vehicle, it was armed with a 50 mm KwK 38 L/42 gun. Later models were upgraded with a more powerful 50 mm KwK 39 L/60 gun to meet evolving battlefield demands. However, as the war progressed and Germany encountered heavier Soviet tanks like the T-34 and KV-1, the Panzer III-J began to struggle. By 1943, it was largely outclassed on the Eastern Front due to its relatively light armor and limited firepower, especially compared to newer German tanks like the Panzer IV and Panther. As a result, many Panzer III-J tanks were either phased out or relegated to secondary roles, such as infantry support or training. Production of the Panzer III ended in 1943, but the Sturmgeschütz III assault gun, developed from the Panzer III chassis, continued to be manufactured until the end of the war.","faction":"Germany","type":"tank","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_panzer_iii_j_late","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_panzer_iii_j_late_title","SourceString":"PANZER III-J LATE","LocalizedString":"PANZER III-J LATE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_panzer_iii_j_late_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran when the enemy HQ has taken 4 or more damage.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran when the enemy HQ has taken 4 or more damage."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_panzer_iii_j_late_history","SourceString":"The Panzer III Ausf. J was the most common variant of the Panzer III, a German medium tank widely used in WWII. Initially designed as an anti-tank vehicle, it was armed with a 50 mm KwK 38 L/42 gun. Later models were upgraded with a more powerful 50 mm KwK 39 L/60 gun to meet evolving battlefield demands. However, as the war progressed and Germany encountered heavier Soviet tanks like the T-34 and KV-1, the Panzer III-J began to struggle. By 1943, it was largely outclassed on the Eastern Front due to its relatively light armor and limited firepower, especially compared to newer German tanks like the Panzer IV and Panther. As a result, many Panzer III-J tanks were either phased out or relegated to secondary roles, such as infantry support or training. Production of the Panzer III ended in 1943, but the Sturmgeschütz III assault gun, developed from the Panzer III chassis, continued to be manufactured until the end of the war.","LocalizedString":"The Panzer III Ausf. J was the most common variant of the Panzer III, a German medium tank widely used in WWII. Initially designed as an anti-tank vehicle, it was armed with a 50 mm KwK 38 L/42 gun. Later models were upgraded with a more powerful 50 mm KwK 39 L/60 gun to meet evolving battlefield demands. However, as the war progressed and Germany encountered heavier Soviet tanks like the T-34 and KV-1, the Panzer III-J began to struggle. By 1943, it was largely outclassed on the Eastern Front due to its relatively light armor and limited firepower, especially compared to newer German tanks like the Panzer IV and Panther. As a result, many Panzer III-J tanks were either phased out or relegated to secondary roles, such as infantry support or training. Production of the Panzer III ended in 1943, but the Sturmgeschütz III assault gun, developed from the Panzer III chassis, continued to be manufactured until the end of the war."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardS